Morning both,

Quick note before I head out. Two things going on for us.

Ledburry - as per the LRF report, water is into properties on Bye Street. I've
been down there this morning, it's worse than the 12 properties in the report,
I'd say 18 or 19 including the two shops on the corner. Community hall is open
and the WI have got tea on. Still no power to the far end of Woodleigh Rd.

Separately and unrelated, we've got surface water flooding in Bromyard, mainly
the industrial estate off Leominster Road. No properties affected, but the
estate is inaccessible and a couple of businesses can't open. Drainage team a=
re
aware. Low priority compared to Ledbury but wanted it on your radar.

Also worth flagging - Environment Agency have a flood alert (not warning) for
the Frome at Bishop's Frome, nothing happening yet.

Gareth

